{"name":"Statuary","hex":"#9ea4a5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"statuary","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The craft of making statues.","Statues considered collectively."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who makes or deals in statues."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/statuary"}],"entries":[{"title":"Statue","blocks":[{"text":"A statue is a free-standing sculpture in which the realistic, full-length figures of persons or animals are carved or cast in a durable material such as wood, metal, glass, marble, or stone. Typical statues are life-sized or close to life-size. A sculpture that represents persons or animals in full figure, but that is small enough to lift and carry is a statuette or figurine, whilst those that are more than twice life-size are regarded as colossal statues."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Lincoln_Memorial_statue_at_night_2011.jpg/330px-Lincoln_Memorial_statue_at_night_2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Statue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Urfa_man.jpg/500px-Urfa_man.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Urfa_man.jpg/500px-Urfa_man.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Urfa Man, a 1.80 metres (5 ft 11 in) of standstone developed in c. 9,000 BC and now housed at Şanlıurfa Museum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUrfa_man.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Queen_Hatshepsut%2C_1479-1458_BCE_%28GEM%29.jpg/500px-Queen_Hatshepsut%2C_1479-1458_BCE_%28GEM%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Queen_Hatshepsut%2C_1479-1458_BCE_%28